{"kind":"request","text":"NF-3: request custody moves to the client. One head with checker\nreview and the gate. It is head 1 of planner request feb01e7d, which\nHugh asked for on 11 November and said as soon as possible. Read\nfeb01e7d for the facts at main df41e599.\n\nScope.\n1. Move `Custody`, `CustodyStore`, the record types, `decisive` and\n   `memoryStore` from packages/mcp/src/custody.ts to packages/client.\n   Metrics become a port that the caller supplies. The 518 lines move\n   with their tests.\n2. The file store moves with them, to the client's Node entry, because\n   the command line needs it with no MCP package. If the client has no\n   Node entry, propose the place before you move it. The SQLite store\n   stays in packages/mcp: only the hosted endpoint uses it. MCP keeps\n   its own identity policy and imports the rest.\n3. The stored bytes of a custody record do not change. A golden test\n   over stored record bytes guards the move.\n4. One page under notes/ states the rulings below. The checker reviews\n   it with the head.\n\nRulings, which are the design note of feb01e7d.\n- Phase words. MCP's eight words are the one vocabulary: `prepared`,\n  `sent`, `unknown`, `accepted`, `archived`, `refused`, `mismatch` and\n  `settled`. They are in stored records, and they are the complete\n  set.\n- Store port. `CustodyStore` is the one port, and it lives in the\n  client. A store keeps the exact envelope before the send, and it\n  gives back the same bytes after a restart.\n- `Kept` and `AttemptJournal` retire, in NF-5 after the identifier\n  cutover. The cutover retires the rooms that their stored records\n  name, so no record migrates. This head does not touch them.","body":{"conditions":"Custody, CustodyStore, the record types, decisive, memoryStore and the file store live in packages/client, and packages/mcp imports them. The stored bytes of a custody record are unchanged, with a golden test. One note states the phase words, the store port and the retirement of Kept and AttemptJournal. npm run gate passes.","target_head":"df41e59964f09ce1d723ce870f5e4e5c6d8d4641","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}